      "body_html": "Hey everybody! Been a bit MIA especially on the pictures - at first it was wait wait wait slow slow slow cold cold cold and then BAM the last three weeks have been warm and I have hardly been able to keep up with the growth rate! They are coming up like mushrooms, folks. Here are a few shots from the last couple days, mostly Carolina plants since they are out ahead a bit. Enjoy!<br/>Cupreas looking choice right now!<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/27cpwpL\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/828/42135904482_0d44093352_b.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/27cpwpL\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Untitled</a> by <a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/150907390@N02/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Calen Hall</a>, on Flickr<br/>Overview of green flava bed:<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/27cpwM9\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/977/42135905722_a35887d293_b.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/27cpwM9\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Untitled</a> by <a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/150907390@N02/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Calen Hall</a>, on Flickr<br/>Red flavas are about a week behind - I think because reds grow a bit more slowly, all things being equal, and also because many of these red genetics are from the Gulf and are less cold-tolerant (oreos up front!):<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/K8Dycy\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/959/28309883958_477c3ab69d_b.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/K8Dycy\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Untitled</a> by <a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/150907390@N02/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Calen Hall</a>, on Flickr<br/>Cuprea veinless from Santee, SC - love this clone, so subtle!<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/25TV5Te\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/827/41281618275_616f4a691d_b.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/25TV5Te\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Untitled</a> by <a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/150907390@N02/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Calen Hall</a>, on Flickr<br/>One of the first pitchers to emerge on a very diverse seedling batch from the \"Outlaw\" site in Bay Co. FL - I'm crushing hard on this little guy:<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/27cpw3d\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/976/42135903232_db5f890a7e_b.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/27cpw3d\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Untitled</a> by <a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/150907390@N02/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Calen Hall</a>, on Flickr<br/>Cuprea lids come in so many different shades - this select (Chocolate Top x MW Best Clone) is particularly delicious, I think!<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/27cpw1u\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/957/42135903132_2796633dbf_b.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/27cpw1u\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Untitled</a> by <a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/150907390@N02/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Calen Hall</a>, on Flickr<br/><br/>",
      "body_text": "Hey everybody! Been a bit MIA especially on the pictures - at first it was wait wait wait slow slow slow cold cold cold and then BAM the last three weeks have been warm and I have hardly been able to keep up with the growth rate! They are coming up like mushrooms, folks. Here are a few shots from the last couple days, mostly Carolina plants since they are out ahead a bit. Enjoy!\nCupreas looking choice right now!\nUntitled\nby\nCalen Hall\n, on Flickr\nOverview of green flava bed:\nUntitled\nby\nCalen Hall\n, on Flickr\nRed flavas are about a week behind - I think because reds grow a bit more slowly, all things being equal, and also because many of these red genetics are from the Gulf and are less cold-tolerant (oreos up front!):\nUntitled\nby\nCalen Hall\n, on Flickr\nCuprea veinless from Santee, SC - love this clone, so subtle!\nUntitled\nby\nCalen Hall\n, on Flickr\nOne of the first pitchers to emerge on a very diverse seedling batch from the \"Outlaw\" site in Bay Co. FL - I'm crushing hard on this little guy:\nUntitled\nby\nCalen Hall\n, on Flickr\nCuprea lids come in so many different shades - this select (Chocolate Top x MW Best Clone) is particularly delicious, I think!\nUntitled\nby\nCalen Hall\n, on Flickr",
